@startuml domain-model
' ============================================================
' Internet Bookstore — Domain Model
'
' Single project-wide diagram. Continuously updated:
'   - Initial pass: Product Owner + Analyst, time-boxed ~2 h, BEFORE any UC text.
'   - Updated by Analyst whenever robustness analysis discovers a new entity.
'   - Re-validated at every M1 (REQ↔UC↔domain) and M2 (UC↔RB↔domain) gate.
'
' ICONIX domain model rules:
'   1. Real-world objects only — no GUI classes (pages, screens, buttons).
'   2. Not a data model — no database tables, no DTOs.
'   3. = project glossary — every entity name must match the term in UC text.
'   4. Show only is-a / has-a relationships that exist in the real world.
'   5. Time-boxed and incomplete by design — it evolves through robustness analysis.
'   6. Will not match the final class diagram — that is expected.
'
' Attributes only (no operations).
' ============================================================

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam DefaultFontName "Helvetica"

' ── Actors of the bookstore (people in the real world) ─────
class Customer {
  + name : String
  + emailAddress : String
}

class Moderator {
  + staffId : String
  + name : String
}

class Editor {
  + staffId : String
}

' ── Catalogue ─────────────────────────────────────────────
class Book {
  + isbn : String
  + title : String
  + author : String
  + publisher : String
  + price : Money
}

class Catalog {
  + name : String
}

' ── Reviews (the part this thread is about) ───────────────
abstract class Review {
  + body : String
  + rating : Integer    ' 1..5 stars
  + submittedAt : Date
  + state : ReviewState ' Pending | Published | Rejected
}

class CustomerReview {
  ' Reader-submitted review.
  ' Title length and review length rules live on this class
  ' (validation enforced via DataAnnotations + IValidatableObject — see BS-ADR-001).
  + title : String
}

class EditorialReview {
  ' Staff-written review. Out of scope for BS-UC-001 but kept here
  ' to make the is-a relationship visible in the domain.
  + headline : String
}

' ── Sessions and queues ───────────────────────────────────
class CustomerSession {
  + isLoggedIn : Boolean
  + lastActivity : Timestamp
}

class PendingReviewsQueue {
  + size : Integer
}

' ── Relationships ─────────────────────────────────────────

' Generalisation (is-a)
CustomerReview  --|> Review
EditorialReview --|> Review

' Aggregation / association (has-a)
Customer "1"   --o "0..*" CustomerReview     : "writes"
Book     "1"   --o "0..*" Review             : "is reviewed by"
Catalog  "1"   --o "0..*" Book               : "lists"
Editor   "1"   --o "0..*" EditorialReview    : "writes"
Customer "0..1" --o "0..1" CustomerSession   : "is bound to"
PendingReviewsQueue "1" --o "0..*" CustomerReview : "holds"
Moderator "1" --o "0..*" CustomerReview      : "approves / rejects"

note bottom of Review
  Note: Review is the abstract glossary term.
  Concrete types (CustomerReview, EditorialReview)
  exist because the bookstore domain treats reader
  reviews and editorial reviews as the same thing
  on the book detail page but different things in
  the moderation pipeline.
end note

note bottom of CustomerReview
  Discovered during robustness analysis of BS-UC-001:
    - "title" attribute added by BS-CI-001 (2026-05-04).
    - All other attributes were present in the
      Sarah-Patel intake interview (2026-04-16).

  Validation rules (BS-BR-001..003) are documented on
  the requirement and exercised by BS-TC-002, BS-TC-003,
  BS-TC-005, BS-TC-020.
end note

@enduml
